{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"ADR LQ / EQ Exemption Check"},"description":"Whether dangerous goods qualify for ADR Limited Quantity (LQ, ADR 3.4) or Excepted Quantity (EQ, ADR 3.5) relief, item by item. Send mode (\"lq\" or \"eq\") and 1-20 items, each with un_number, quantity per INNER packaging (not the whole load) and unit (ml or L for liquids, g or kg for solids); inner_packaging_qty adds the EQ per-outer check. A mass against a volume limit (or the reverse) cannot be compared: that item is inconclusive \u2014 send the unit given by lq_limit_unit. A UN number whose Table A rows disagree needs packing_group or variant_index, else no verdict for it (AMBIGUOUS_UN_VARIANT with candidates[]). For the 1.1.3.6 load-points route use adr_exemption_calculator; for the per-substance LQ/EQ values and variant_index adr_lookup. edition (\"2025\" | \"2027\") and as_of choose the ADR edition; neither sent, ADR 2025 until 2027-01-01. Fields are checked by name: a field the tool does not read is refused with a tool error naming it and listing the accepted ones, never ignored. Rate-limited: a limit error carries reset_at, the UTC time the allowance resets. A quantity-threshold check only \u2014 packaging, marking and documentation conformity are not assessed; not legal advice, verify against the current UNECE ADR text.","execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"as_of":{"description":"The date the answer is for, YYYY-MM-DD (default today, UTC).","pattern":"^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$","type":"string"},"edition":{"description":"ADR edition; wins over as_of. Omitted: as_of picks it.","enum":["2025","2027"],"type":"string"},"items":{"description":"Items to check (1-20 per call).","items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"inner_packaging_qty":{"description":"EQ mode only: inner packagings pe